# Normalize line endings on checkout.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true smudges CRLF into the working tree while Go
# write-back tooling (gofmt -w, and the lefthook pre-commit hook that runs it on
# staged files) rewrites the same files back to LF. The result is a standing set
# of phantom-modified files whose `git diff` is empty, which blocks `git merge`
# with "local changes would be overwritten" on files that have no changes.
#
# It also keeps shell scripts and golden fixtures LF in the working tree.
# scripts/*.sh run under bash on Linux and CI, where a CRLF shebang fails with
# "bad interpreter"; scripts/golden.sh compares fixtures with byte-exact
# `diff -u`, so a CRLF working copy makes every text fixture appear to differ.
#
# Safe to add without a renormalization commit: every text blob committed here
# is already stored LF (`git ls-files --eol` reports no i/crlf and no i/mixed),
# so this changes only checkout smudging, never a stored byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored build cache — leave its bytes exactly as committed.
.gocache/** -text
CHANGELOG.md text eol=lf
